**Zurkrieg** (Heroic). A self-made tycoon and fighter who hunts the
world's most powerful people to recruit or destroy them. Grant
Zurkrieg grew up poor in Europe and has craved power ever since. A
gift for economics made him a millionaire by his mid-twenties; when
money wasn't enough, he built his body into a fighting machine, and
that wasn't enough either. Now his Men in Black scour the world for
its most powerful people, so that he can make them join him or crush
them. *Attack +3 (Power & Control), Combat Expert +3, Evasive +2,
Intimidating +3, Iron-Willed +2, Knowledge +4 (Economics), Minions +4
(Men in Black), Smart +2, Strong +3, Tough +2, Wealthy +5; Arrogant
−2, Code of Conduct −1 (Must Have Fair Duels), Fear −3 (Drowning, from
Childhood Accident), Hatred −2 (Weakness), Obsession −3 (Power),
Secret −3 (Illegal Research), Stubborn −3.* Extending Cane (Reach;
Weapon): Roll 5, DX 7, End 0. Zurkrieg's cane is engineered to extend,
giving him command of any situation. The World's Strongest (Stunning;
Ineffective, Unwieldy): Roll 5, DX 6, End 0. While fond enough of his
cane, Zurkrieg enjoys finishing off opponents barehanded. Defense 4.
Health 60, Endurance 40. TV 18.

Zurkrieg's **Men in Black** are cyborgs, assembled from the terminally
ill, the brain-dead, and even the dead: part human, part machine.
They're slow but tireless and strong, and they carry out his orders
exactly. *Strong +2, Tough +2; Emotionless −3, Servitude −3, Slow −1.*

